                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 15.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-4",
                                                    "linecount": 7,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 85.0, 983.0, 133.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_linecount": 7,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 8.0, 53.0, 968.0, 133.0 ],
                                                    "text": "The routing matrix is used to route the output of the various instruments to the available effects and to the main output. The output of the modules on the left is connected to the input of the modules on the right. The audio effects (Roar, Reverb and Delay) are routed to the main output by default. The two Scylla modules have a \"Mod\" inlet that is used for frequency and phase modulation. \n\nA connection between two modules can be either fixed or dynamic. For dynamic connections, the connection gain is controlled either through direct modulation (from any of the T-Stick features, displayed in blue) or predicted by a neural network (displayed in purple, see the neural network reference for more infos). All three types of connections can coexist in a single performance patch.",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
