                                                    "id": "obj-9",
                                                    "index": 1,
                                                    "maxclass": "inlet",
                                                    "numinlets": 0,
                                                    "numoutlets": 1,
                                                    "outlettype": [ "" ],
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 68.0, 1.0, 30.0, 30.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 15.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-4",
                                                    "linecount": 27,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 85.0, 980.0, 493.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_linecount": 27,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 8.0, 53.0, 964.0, 493.0 ],
                                                    "text": "The three neural networks in this section are used to define the mappings between T-Stick features and sound parameters: the \"Mapping by Demonstration\" approach allows to define these mappings by demonstrating the physical gesture while hearing the sound. The neural network automatically learns the relationship between motion features and sound parameters based on these recorded examples.\n\nThere are three neural networks available, each of which can use a specific subset of the motion features. Note that once a network is trained on a specific feature set, this cannot be changed unless the model is first reset.\n\nBefore a gesture can be recorded, make sure that the \"Sound Gesture\" tab is set to the ID of the neural network you intend to use, and that there is at least one active connection in the assignment matrix. The connections define the parameters that will be predicted by a specific network (see Assignment Matrix reference for more infos). Once a network is trained, the connections associated with it cannot be changed unless the model is cleared first.\n\nAt this point, you should be hearing a time-varying sound (depending on the modulation from the LFOs). Make sure that the T-Stick is enabled in the \"T-Stick\" tab and that it's currently sending data, and select what features you want to use for the current neural network.\nYou can now toggle \"Record Gesture\" and perform it with the T-Stick while listening to the sound. There is no fixed rule to how long the recording should be; a single example of 1 or 2 seconds is usually enough. \n\nAfter at least one gesture is recorded, the neural network is ready to be trained. Toggle the \"Train NN\" button and leave it on until the error seems to stop decreasing significantly. Anything below 0.1 should work fine, but it really depends on the case.\n\nNow the model is ready to make predictions. Turn on the \"Predict\" toggle and perform the gesture with the T-Stick. The model will begin predicting parameter values based on the input features, and you will hear the sound gesture as you perform. Increasing the \"smooth\" parameter applies a low pass filter to the predicted output vector, making it more stable but also less reactive.\n\nMultiple gestures can be recorded to a single neural network by recording in separate instances. However the input and output features must stay the same across the dataset, so you can't change the feature selection and the assignment matrix between different recordings (unless the model is cleared first). Any added recordings require the model to be re-trained to take effect.",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-2",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 308.0, 45.0, 386.0, 35.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 304.0, 4.0, 372.0, 35.0 ],
                                                    "prototypename": "SubComm",
                                                    "text": "NEURAL NETWORKS REFERENCE",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 0.28627450980392155, 0.28627450980392155, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            }
