                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 18.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-1",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 416.5, 737.0, 176.0, 28.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 402.5, 745.0, 176.0, 28.0 ],
                                                    "prototypename": "SubComm",
                                                    "text": "TROUBLESHOOTING",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 0.28627450980392155, 0.7294117647058823, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 15.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                                    "linecount": 2,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 761.0, 969.0, 42.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_linecount": 2,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 9.0, 775.0, 979.0, 42.0 ],
                                                    "text": "If you have connections in the assignment matrix but you're not hearing the modulations, make sure the global \"Modulation\" toggle is turned on. \nIf you still can't hear it, make sure that the instrument is actually being sent to output in the \"Routing\" section, and that the volume is turned on.",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 18.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-7",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 396.0, 364.0, 217.0, 28.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 377.5, 365.0, 212.0, 28.0 ],
                                                    "prototypename": "SubComm",
                                                    "text": "Defining a Sound Gesture",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 0.28627450980392155, 0.7294117647058823, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 15.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-8",
                                                    "linecount": 19,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 9.0, 386.0, 993.0, 349.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_linecount": 19,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 8.0, 395.0, 966.0, 349.0 ],
                                                    "text": "A sound gesture is defined by assigning one or more LFO to any of the available sound parameters; the resulting modulation will define the sonic character of the gesture learned by the neural network. You can therefore expect that performing a learned gesture with the T-Stick will produce parameter curves whose range is similar to the one defined through the assignment matrix. The range of each modulation can be set through the number boxes besides each parameter. \n\nBefore a sound gesture can be defined, choose which of the three neural networks will be used to record it through the \"Sound Gesture\" selector tab. The \"global\" tab is used to set fixed modulations, that are not used to train the neural networks but will be output as fixed parameter modulations on top of the learned gestures. The connections defined while on this tab can therefore be considered as fixed LFO modulations that will be added to the predicted values from the models.\n\nWhen a gesture is selected, the connections made through the assignment matrix and their range define what sound parameters that model will control and how much. Once a neural network is trained on a gesture, the assignment matrix for that gesture cannot be changed (unless the NN is first reset). However multiple gestures can be recorded using the same parameter set. \nA single parameter can also be controlled by multiple gestures. When more than two or more NNs control the same parameter, the final value will be a proportional normalisation of all the contributions at each inference step.\n\nA single gesture can include as many parameters as one desires, even from different instruments. However it would be best practice to limit each model to a few musically meaningful parameters, in order to avoid confusion.\nAfter a sound gesture is defined, it can be associated to a T-Stick gesture through the models. See the neural network reference for more infos.",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 18.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-6",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 463.0, 220.0, 83.0, 28.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 442.0, 191.0, 83.0, 28.0 ],
                                                    "prototypename": "SubComm",
                                                    "text": "The LFOs",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 0.28627450980392155, 0.7294117647058823, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 15.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-5",
                                                    "linecount": 6,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 247.0, 987.0, 115.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_linecount": 7,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 8.0, 221.0, 964.0, 133.0 ],
                                                    "text": "There are three stereo LFOs that can be used to define the sound gestures, each with its own independent parameters.\n\nThe \"stereo\" parameter controls the phase shift between the two LFO channels, while \"detune\" applies a little frequency variation to each channel. If the LFO is connected to a mono parameter, only the left channel is used. \n\nThe other parameters set the LFO shape, allowing a great range of possible modulations in order to provide many different types of sound gestures.",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 15.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-4",
                                                    "linecount": 7,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 85.0, 980.0, 133.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_linecount": 7,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 8.0, 53.0, 964.0, 133.0 ],
                                                    "text": "In order for a neural network to learn associations between motion features and parameter values, it needs to be provided with a set of example associations to use as training data. \n\nIn this mapping by demonstration approach, the performer defines a sound gesture as a set of parameter modulations, specified by connecting the three available LFOs to any of the available sound parameters using the assignment matrix. The result is an evolving soundscape, that can be associated with a performance gesture through the neural networks. For more information on how to record gestures and train the models, please see the neural network reference.",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-2",
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 308.0, 45.0, 386.0, 35.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 290.0, 4.0, 386.0, 35.0 ],
                                                    "prototypename": "SubComm",
                                                    "text": "ASSIGNMENT MATRIX REFERENCE",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 0.28627450980392155, 0.28627450980392155, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "lines": [
                                            {
                                                "patchline": {
