                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 15.0,
                                                    "id": "obj-4",
                                                    "linecount": 18,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 85.0, 426.0, 331.0 ],
                                                    "presentation": 1,
                                                    "presentation_linecount": 18,
                                                    "presentation_rect": [ 8.0, 53.0, 426.0, 331.0 ],
                                                    "text": "Here all the features extracted from the T-Stick are displayed:\n- The \"brush\" gesture is the finger position along the capacitive sensor. The speed of the brush is also available.\n- The FSR pressure level (normalised).\n- The T-Stick's angular velocity (Yaw Pitch Roll).\n- Orientation, both as Yaw Pitch Roll and quaternion. The quaternion is used in the neural networks because it avoids the -pi/pi wrap and Gimball lock problems; the YPR orientation is used to explore the CE-Matcher's corpus space.\n- A global activation feature, calculated as the RMS of the FSR, angular velocity and brush speed. A Schmidtt trigger on this global activation function starts and stops the recording of the trigger gestures (after the \"record\" button is first pressed).\n\nAll of these features can be independently smoothed (besides quaternion, since it's already filtered in the firmware), and are displayed through the curves below.",
                                                    "textcolor": [ 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0 ]
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "fontface": 1,
                                                    "fontname": "Ableton Sans Medium",
                                                    "fontsize": 24.0,
